            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 839,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "`schemas/virtual_sensor.json` does not define a `Purpose` property.\n\nAnd i did not find any linked patch / gerrit topic.\n\n\n\nIf this gets merged as-is, it means upstream boards will not be able to configure the feature, right?\n\n\nDo we need to get the `Purpose` property added to that EM schema."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 839,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pedro Maione",
                        "email": "pedro.maione@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pmaione"
                    },
                    "message": "Indeed, for configuring it via EM we will need to add the Purpose property to the `virtual_sensor.json` schema. \n\nThis was actually intended to be used with a include json config file from the recipe bbappend, as stated in the example (that's a bit outdated) and I added the EM support to allow the newer approach for configuration.\n\nMy idea was that, merging this, I could propose the schema patch later."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 839,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> This was actually intended to be used with a include json config file from the recipe bbappend,\n\nI don't like incompatible alternatives.\n\n And in this case we don't require that, right? We can just create a separate patch for the schema and then merge+bump both at the same time.\n\n\nOtherwise, maybe someone will block the EM schema patch and then we would have a feature that only works in one configuration style, preventing folks from migrating to the preferred configuration style (IMO that's EM based configuration)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 839,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pedro Maione",
                        "email": "pedro.maione@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pmaione"
                    },
                    "message": "That's better. Will fix this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 839,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pedro Maione",
                        "email": "pedro.maione@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pmaione"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/virtualSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 844,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
